          "email": "jsimmons@infradead.org",
          "date": "2026-08-27 14:25:00.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-9680 utils: handle very large netlink message in liblnetconfig",
        "message": "LU-9680 utils: handle very large netlink message in liblnetconfig\n\nA few scaling patches have exposed a problem in the liblnetconfig\nlibrary when receiving message from kernel space. Currently we\nexamine if the remaining space falls belong a certain level, 1024\nbyte, then we increase the internal buffer size to recieve the\nnext Netlink message. It is possible that the next Netlink message\nis much larger than the remaining 1024 bytes. This patch changes\nit to compares the calculated size needed to fit the unpacked\nNetlink packet into the internal buffer. Be aware the internal\nbuffer consumes more space than the size of the recieved Netlink\npacket so we scale it by 4 which covers most cases. The new\nbuffer size is ensured to be enlarge enough to cover the next\nNetlink packet. A few other issues are addressed as well. Now\ndata->read is correctly preserved which matters for Netlink\nstreaming. On error of realloc() we preserve data->buffer so\nit doesn't leak. Lastly set data->error to -errno which was missed\nfor yaml_netlink_read_handler().\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 985fc4fa2caf (\"LU-14391 utils: handle very large YAML data sets.\")\nSigned-off-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nChange-Id: I60d81bd21496f814b1e8e4884dc4d4a5334fd21c\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
